# chrony per Portitor instance (portitor-chrony@.service). The AppArmor
# profile for chronyd on Debian/Ubuntu only allows /etc/chrony and
# /run/chrony; install.py adds these rules to the profile's local include
# (/etc/apparmor.d/local/usr.sbin.chronyd). The path is the default of
# etc_dir in /etc/portitor/agent.yaml; the PID file is in the unit's
# private /tmp, its command socket under run_dir.
/etc/portitor/instances/*/chrony.conf r,
/tmp/chronyd.pid rw,
/run/portitor/chrony/*/ rw,
/run/portitor/chrony/*/chronyd.sock rw,
